WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.601
-Well, Election Day may be over,

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.437
but the ballot
counting continues,

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.007
with Joe Biden tentatively ahead
in enough states

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.175
to win the presidency
and, as expected,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.777
the president and his allies
are falsely declaring victory,

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.212
lying to discredit the results,

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.814
and trying to stop the count
altogether.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.383
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:21.354
♪♪

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.756
We're taping this at 5:00,
so we can't say what will happen

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.758
as states continue
counting ballots,

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.661
and they should all be counted,
but as we're taping this,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.630
the president's path
to victory is narrowing.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.932
Wisconsin and Michigan
have both been called for Biden

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.401
and, as New York Times
election analyst Nate Cohn

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:36.536
noted, Biden...

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.208
Or, as Trump put it,
in his unhinged,

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.643
middle-of-the-night
complaint fest...

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:47.347
-This is a fraud
on the American public.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:51.150
This is an embarrassment
to our country.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.386
We were getting ready
to win this election.

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:57.356
Frankly,
we did win this election.
[ Cheering ]

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.625
We have won Georgia.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.461
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:10.370
We're up by 2.5%, or 117,000
votes, with only 7% left.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.370
They're never going to catch us.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.939
They can't catch us.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:17.209
Likewise, we've clearly won
North Carolina.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.745
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:23.082
Where we're up 1.4%.

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:27.853
Or 77,000 votes, with only
approximately 5% left.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:28.888
They can't catch us.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.888
-Alright, first of all,

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:31.323
yeah, they can catch you,

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:33.192
since you lumber
like a retired Frankenstein

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.928
looking for a golf ball
in a sand trap.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.763
Second, no,
you haven't won those states.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:40.099
You might win some of them,
once the counting is done,

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:42.368
or you might lose them,
but the counting isn't done.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.703
For example, I don't know what's
going to happen in Georgia,

00:01:44.703 --> 00:01:46.005
but, as we're taping this,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.840
there are more votes to count
in Democratic areas

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.443
and that godforsaken
New York Times needle

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.977
has it tilting toward Biden.

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:54.280
Spent all time staring at that
thing and, every time it moved,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.949
it was like hearing a twig snap
in a horror movie.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:59.552
I feel like that needle
is a murder's ice pick

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.921
that I'm just trying
to keep away from my eye.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.456
It's a big deal
that Trump and Biden

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.091
are even neck-and-neck
in Georgia,

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.425
and Trump knows that

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:07.827
because, in the final days
of the campaign,

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.362
he was whining that he even had
to campaign there at all.

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:11.631
-I shouldn't even be here.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.632
They say I have Georgia made.

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:16.035
-Wow, what are a shock
you're underperforming there.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.238
[ As Trump ]
I shouldn't even be
in this backwater state,

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.006
you swamp people.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:23.443
When my campaign manager told me
we were going to Georgia,

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.644
I said, "Georgia?!

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:27.080
With those redneck yokels.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.917
Don't those people eat rocks
and drink gasoline?"

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:34.753
Anyway, vote for me,
if you can figure out how

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:37.690
to sign your name on the ballot,
you freaks."

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.725
In fact, as we speak,
Trump's campaign is asking

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.828
for a recount in Wisconsin
and spent all night fighting

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:45.498
with Fox News to withdraw their
call for Biden in Arizona.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.766
And you know Trump's
in bad shape

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.167
when he's fighting
with Fox News,

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.403
an entire network dedicated
to repeating everything he says.

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:54.206
That's like the Kardashians
fighting with E!

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:56.475
I'm told.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:58.477
So, in those states,
Trump wants to keep counting,

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.245
but, in early states
where early return had him up,

00:03:00.245 --> 00:03:02.414
like Pennsylvania,
he's trying to stop ballots

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.550
from being counting
and suggested

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.786
he wanted the Supreme Court
to help him steal it.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.390
-We'll going
to the U.S. Supreme Court.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.593
We want all voting to stop.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.561
-You can't just go
to the Supreme Court

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.730
and tell them to stop counting.
That's not a thing.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.365
Trump talks about it like
he's just going to

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.834
walk down the street
and knock on their door.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.102
[ As Trump ]
Hello, is Brett there?

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.371
We're drinking beers
with Tobin and Squee.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.506
This is deeply dangerous
authoritarian behavior

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.109
and a major test
for the national media.
We have to resist this.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.244
Trump's logic here is obvious.
It's grotesque.

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:33.813
He wants to keep counting
Trump votes,

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.114
but stop counting Biden votes.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.283
If he had his way,
he'd get to personally sift

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.585
through every ballot
and cross out Biden's name.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:42.622
So, as of this taping,
they're still counting ballots.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.156
We're still awaiting results,
but, as we said,

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.626
the path for Biden looks much
better than the path for Trump,

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:49.528
which is why Trump and his
allies on Fox are going all out

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:51.697
to falsely declare victory
and discredit the results.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.966
But, first, let's retrace

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.901
what happened last night
and how we got here.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.837
If you were a Democrat
or a sane person

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.639
hoping for an early landslide,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.307
as we all know,
that did not happen.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.275
In fact, Democrats' hopes
for an obvious,

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:06.546
overwhelming result early in the
night were quickly dashed

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.248
in a state where Democrats'
hopes are always dashed,

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:10.783
the state that has toyed with

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.452
and tormented Democrats
for years,

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.920
the Loki of swing states...

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:15.989 line:0%
The state ping-ponged

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.023 line:0%
back and forth for a while,

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.092 line:0%
until it eventually became clear

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.759 line:0%
it would not go Biden's way.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:21.761 line:0%
-Welcome to the
roller coaster

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.761 line:0%
that is Florida.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:23.763 line:0%
If you're look at Florida

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.265 line:0%
right now,
it's a roller coaster.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.966 line:0%
Welcome back to the
roller coaster.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.167 line:0%
Joe Biden has pulled ahead

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.236 line:0%
by 7,784 votes

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.503 line:0%
in the state of Florida.

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:33.038 line:0%
-Trump just took the lead
in Florida.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.440 line:0%
-Again, this is going to be
a roller coaster

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.309 line:0%
by 28,000 votes, right?

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.309 line:0%
Palm Beach turned blue.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:38.444 line:0%
It is red at the moment.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.012 line:0%
It the has gone back
and forth several times,

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.547 line:0%
in just the last 15
or 20 minute.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.582 line:0%
Let's take a look at Florida
as we go through it.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.485 line:0%
Again, this one is
always a roller coaster.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:47.720
-Stop calling it
a roller coaster.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.555
If you're going to be
on TV for 14 hours,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.525
learn like a second word
to describe up and down.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.559
We know it's a roller coaster.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:54.960
Every time,
we look forward to it,

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.696
then, we experience
abject terror

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.866
and we end up barfing in a trash
can and say never again.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:02.134
And Florida isn't one
of those roller coasters

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.403
at a legit theme park.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.738
It's one of the weird,
traveling carnivals

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.473
where none of the rides
have safety bars

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.810
and the petting zoo animals
are just two donkeys and a dog.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.578
[ Gruffly ]
Don't touch the dog.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.480
Why is it that every election
starts with Democrats

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.649
getting hopeful about Florida
and then getting burned?

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:17.750
It's the political equivalent

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.051
of that kid
from "The Twilight Zone."

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.654
We're begging him not
to send us to the cornfield

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.823
and then, he smiles for a second
and we breathe a sigh of relief

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:26.158
and then, he points to us

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.127
and sends us
to the goddamn cornfield.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.795
And then, they are wandering
around the cornfield,

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.731
saying, "Nate Silver said
this wouldn't happen!"

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.032
And then, Nate Silver says,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.201
"No, I said this probably
wouldn't happen."

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.102
And then we scream,
"Not now, Nate!

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.570
I'm corn!"

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.739
We were fold Biden
had a 90% chance of winning,

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:43.142
that the polling had been
consistent for an entire year,

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.210
that he was going to win
by like eight points.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.712
The early returns
felt like a put-on,

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.480
like some sort
of elaborate joke.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.450 line:0%
-Election night
in America,

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.220 line:0%
brought to you
by "Borat Subsequent Moviefilm."

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.321
-Damn it!

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.789
He did it again.
He's so good.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.926
John King was Sasha Baron Cohen
the whole time, wasn't he?

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.761
I should've guessed when he said
Democrats were underperforming

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:06.098
in the crucial Wisconsin county
of Wawaweewa!

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:09.801
[ Laughter ]
Suffice it to say
election night was not fun.

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:12.505
After one state, I was already
deep into the whiskey

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.973
and my stomach felt
like Chernobyl.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.574
Who could possibly enjoy this?

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:17.209
-This is why elections are fun.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.878
-Oh, right, people who are

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.913
completely unaffected
by the outcome.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.916
John King, I assure you, you
were the only one having fun.

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.885
That's like hearing
your surgeon lean over,

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.686
right before putting you under,
and saying,

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:29.722
"This is why
brain surgery is fun.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.090
Oh, whoa!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.191
I did not see that on the scan."

00:06:33.191 --> 00:06:34.593
Another thing to remember

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:36.829
is that these anxiety-filled
election nights

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.464
are a completely unnecessary
product of two things --

00:06:39.464 --> 00:06:41.701
cable TV
and the electoral college.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.804
If we just had a national
popular vote,

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.839
like a sane country,
we wouldn't have to come up

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.106
with all this complicated math

00:06:48.106 --> 00:06:50.276
to fend off unpopular
fascist demagogues

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.244
and we wouldn't have
to learn the names

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:55.414
of all 254 counties in Texas
where, somehow,

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:57.983
there's always more
Trump votes left to come in.

00:06:57.983 --> 00:06:59.151
"As you can see here,

00:06:59.151 --> 00:07:01.087
Biden doing well
in Stonefield County,

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.654
but over here
in Dinkington County,

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:05.023
we're expecting about 6 million
more Trump votes,

00:07:05.023 --> 00:07:06.291
so, keep an eye on that."

00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:08.160
And, at some point,
even the cable shows

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.430
that thrive on this contrived
drama ran out of stuff to say,

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.365
leading to moments like this --

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:14.566 line:0%
-You see a lot of red,
but you see

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:15.735 line:0%
a lot of blue
as well.

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.102
-Oh! Thanks, Wolf.

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:18.303
Are you a news analyst

00:07:18.303 --> 00:07:19.872
or a tour guide
at the Guggenheim?

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:22.007
[ As Blitzer ]
There's a lot of red
and also a lot of blue

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:23.009
and over there

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.611
is one neon light on a wall.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.412
So last night did not
start well for Democrats,

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:28.614
but we should've expected that.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.983
We were told for weeks
that's what would happen,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:32.017
that, because of mail ballots,

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.319
there would be
a red-to-blue shift,

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:34.753
that Republicans would look
good early and then,

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.522
Democrats would gain overnight,
and, yet,

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.423
we couldn't heed our own advice.

00:07:38.423 --> 00:07:39.758
It's like walking into a casino

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:41.661
telling yourself you're going
to play one game of craps

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.996
and then, an hour later,
you're trying to sell your watch

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.865
to a parking valet
for 10 more chips.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:48.534
This exact same thing
happened in 2018,

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.135 line:0%
when Democrats
ultimately beat Republicans

00:07:50.135 --> 00:07:52.471 line:0%
by a record margin
and won a huge majority.

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:53.939 line:0%
Remember how that night started?

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:55.774 line:0%
Democrats lost races in Florida

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.443 line:0%
and this is
how everyone reacted.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:59.578 line:0%
-When you look at what's
going on here tonight,

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:01.413 line:0%
this is not
a blue wave.

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:03.749 line:0%
-This is not a blue wave.
-It is not a blue wave.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.352 line:0%
-It's nothing like a blue wave
or a tidal wave.
-Right.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.921 line:0%
-It's not a blue wave.
-So we haven't seen
the blue wave.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:10.423 line:0%
-There is not a blue wave.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:11.990
-Which, in retrospect,
was wrong.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.559
It was a blue wave,

00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:15.394
with Democrats winning
by a historic margin

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:17.763
and a national repudiation
of Trump and the GOP.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:21.100
Watching all that early punditry
was like watching Jim Nantz

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.235
call the game for the Jets
after the first drive

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:24.737
because they kicked
a field goal.

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:25.838
[ As Nantz ]
Tony, I just don't see how

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.039
the Chiefs come back from this

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:28.307
and I'm sorry.
While I was talking,

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:30.309
the Chiefs have scored
21 points.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.911
Last night, early in the night,
we all started to get

00:08:32.911 --> 00:08:35.514
that queasy feeling that it was
2016 all over again.

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.616
I spent most of the night
clenching so hard,

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:39.284
I have six-pack abs now.

00:08:39.284 --> 00:08:40.285
And, in those moments,
I will say,

00:08:40.285 --> 00:08:41.353
I was very happy that we

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.587
weren't doing a live show.

00:08:42.587 --> 00:08:44.490
It's like no one wants
to have a panic attack,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.024
but, if you're going to,

00:08:46.024 --> 00:08:47.927
you prefer to have it alone
in your apartment,

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:49.862
instead of on the subway,
in hush hour.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.532
But this morning, as millions
of votes actually got counted,

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:54.800
it's starting to feel more
like 2018.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.769
For one thing, Biden is on track

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:58.738
to win a large
popular vote victory,

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:01.941
which would be the seventh time
out of the last eight elections

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:04.009
that the Democrat
won the popular vote.

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:07.813
And, yet, in our ridiculous,
Rube Goldberg political system,

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:09.482
that's just a fun piece
of trivia,

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:11.283
instead of, you know,
the deciding factor.

00:09:11.283 --> 00:09:14.586
